          "title": "You'll want to know: أسرة",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "أسرة — usra — \"a family\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "أسرة (usra) is built on the native Arabic root ʾ-s-r, \"to bind\" (Lane). Lane's usra is a man's nearest kin, named because he is strengthened by them."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
